From: jahshaka <jahshaka@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] clusterlod: a terminal group's border stays locked at every later level

CLUSTER-LOCK-2 (found), CLUSTER-LOCK-3 (landed), 2026-09-29. An upstream
defect in demo/clusterlod.h v1.2 (an upstream PR candidate).
A group whose simplification gets stuck is output as TERMINAL and its
clusters are never merged again. lockBoundary locks a position only when two
groups of the CURRENT level share it, so from the next level on the border
between a terminal group's clusters and a neighbour that keeps simplifying is
an open border of the neighbour's merged mesh: the simplifier may slide it,
and the cut opens between the terminal clusters and the neighbour's coarser
clusters. Measured (atom.cluster_cut, round-bar-40m, once the bake's
displacement lock stopped binding every level): 16 open edges at 4 of the 64
thresholds, all on a terminal group's border.

The fix: every position of a terminal group's clusters is remembered and
locked at every later level. Only positions shared with clusters that are
still pending can matter, so this moves nothing else.
---
--- a/clusterlod.h
+++ b/clusterlod.h
@@ -608,6 +608,10 @@
 
 	std::vector<unsigned char> locks(mesh.vertex_count);
 
+	// positions of clusters in abandoned (terminal) groups; these clusters stay in the output as they are, so their border with
+	// clusters that keep simplifying must stay fixed at every later level (lockBoundary only sees the groups of the current level)
+	std::vector<unsigned char> stuck(mesh.vertex_count);
+
 	// for cluster connectivity, we need a position-only remap that maps vertices with the same position to the same index
 	std::vector<unsigned int> remap(mesh.vertex_count);
 	meshopt_generatePositionRemap(&remap[0], mesh.vertex_positions, mesh.vertex_count, mesh.vertex_positions_stride);
@@ -650,6 +654,9 @@
 		// mark boundaries between groups with a lock bit to avoid gaps in simplified result
 		lockBoundary(locks, groups, clusters, remap, mesh.vertex_lock);
 
+		for (size_t i = 0; i < locks.size(); ++i)
+			locks[i] |= stuck[remap[i]];
+
 		// every group needs to be simplified now
 		for (size_t i = 0; i < groups.size(); ++i)
 		{
@@ -670,6 +677,11 @@
 			{
 				bounds.error = FLT_MAX; // terminal group, won't simplify further
 				outputGroup(config, mesh, clusters, groups[i], bounds, depth, output_context, output_callback);
+
+				for (size_t j = 0; j < groups[i].size(); ++j)
+					for (unsigned int v : clusters[groups[i][j]].indices)
+						stuck[remap[v]] = 1;
+
 				continue; // simplification is stuck; abandon the merge
 			}
 
